				<main id="fsPageContent" class="fsPageContent">
							<h1 class="fsPageTitle">Board Elections</h1>




							<div class="fsPageLayout fsLayout fsOneColumnLayout fsStyleAutoclear" id="fsEl_26606" data-use-new="true" >

				<div class=" fsDiv fsStyleAutoclear" id="fsEl_26607"  >

				<section class="fsElement fsContent" id="fsEl_57799" data-use-new="true" >

				<header>
				<h2 class="fsElementTitle" id="fsElementTitle_57799">Election Links</h2>
	</header>
	<div class="fsElementContent" >
			<div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center;">
<p><a class="button-2" data-file-name="NoticeofWylieISDBoardofTrusteesGeneralElectionBallotDrawing.pdf" data-resource-uuid="a1a9d529-9496-453e-a91d-099143f8e15f" href="/fs/resource-manager/view/a1a9d529-9496-453e-a91d-099143f8e15f" style="margin: 10px;" target="_blank" title="Notice of drawing for place on ballot. Opens in a new window.">Notice of Drawing for Place on Ballot</a></p>

<p><a class="button-3" data-file-name="OrderofElection_2026.pdf" data-resource-uuid="b4267e3e-0d7b-411e-8aa7-ac29c8e6cef3" href="/fs/resource-manager/view/b4267e3e-0d7b-411e-8aa7-ac29c8e6cef3" style="margin: 10px;" target="_blank" title="Order of Election. Opens in a new window.">Order of Election</a></p>

<p><a class="button-4" data-file-name="NoticeOfDeadlineToFileAnApplicationForPlaceOnTheBallot.pdf" data-resource-uuid="85384e84-9fb7-4960-b26a-ebdc89c99c45" href="/fs/resource-manager/view/85384e84-9fb7-4960-b26a-ebdc89c99c45" style="margin: 10px;" target="_blank" title="Notice of Deadline to File Applications for Place on Ballot. Opens in a new window.">Notice of Deadline to File Applications for Place on Ballot</a></p>

<p><a class="button-1" data-file-name="EarlyVotingCalendarExhibitA20261103.pdf" data-resource-uuid="a27c68d2-2cd7-4960-9284-26027eedd9b9" href="/fs/resource-manager/view/a27c68d2-2cd7-4960-9284-26027eedd9b9" style="margin: 10px;" target="_blank" title="2026 early voting calendar [exhibit A]. Opens in a new window.">Early Voting Calendar</a></p>

<p><a class="button-2" data-file-name="ElectionDayLocationsExhibitB20261103.pdf" data-resource-uuid="def7eb48-3916-45b6-9436-a9a842e6e4a0" href="/fs/resource-manager/view/def7eb48-3916-45b6-9436-a9a842e6e4a0" style="margin: 10px;" target="_blank" title="2026 election day locations [exhibit B]. Opens in a new window.">Election Day Locations</a></p>
<!-- HIDE BUTTONS
<p><a class="button-1" data-file-name="NoticeofElection.pdf" data-resource-uuid="eb42331c-a515-468d-aef9-c80ea21e7296" href="/fs/resource-manager/view/eb42331c-a515-468d-aef9-c80ea21e7296" style="margin: 10px;" target="_blank" title="Notice of Trustee General Election. Opens in a new window.">Notice of Trustee General Election</a></p>--></div>


	</div>


	</section>
	
	<section class="fsElement fsContent" id="fsEl_26703" data-use-new="true" >

				<header>
				<h2 class="fsElementTitle" id="fsElementTitle_26703">Board Election Information: November 3, 2026</h2>
	</header>
	<div class="fsElementContent" >
			<h3>About the Board of Trustees</h3>

<p>The Board of Trustees consists of seven members elected to serve, without compensation, for overlapping terms of four years each. Elections are conducted in November. While candidates run for specific places, they represent at large.</p>

<p>The next board of trustee election is scheduled for November 3, 2026. Places up for election will be place 1, place 2, place 5, and place 6.</p>

<p>The school district contracts with Collin County Election Division for election services.</p>

<p><a class="button-6 button-large" href="#candidates">Meet the Candidates</a></p>

<h3>Terms and Election Schedule</h3>

<p>Board members shall be elected for four-year terms, with elections conducted bi-annually, as follows:</p>

<ul>
	<li>The election of four Board members shall be held in 2026, 2030, 2034 and in four-year intervals thereafter.</li>
	<li>The election of three Board members shall be held in 2028, 2032, 2036&nbsp;and in four-year intervals thereafter.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Candidate&#39;s Guide to Primary &amp; General Elections</h3>

<p>The Texas Election Code designates the Secretary of State as the chief election officer of the State of Texas. In order to provide information on the electoral process to all Texans, the&nbsp;office has prepared a guide in the expectation that increased information will result in increased participation.</p>

<p><a href="https://www.sos.state.tx.us/elections/candidates/guide/2026/index.shtml" target="_blank" title="Visit the Secretary of State website. Opens in a new window."><span class="button-2">view the Secretary of state&#39;s website to view the guide</span></a></p>

<h3>2026 Election Highlights</h3>

<ul>
	<li>First day to file for place on the ballot: Saturday, July 18, 2026 <em>(applications will be accepted beginning Monday, July 20, 2026)&nbsp;</em></li>
	<li>Last day to file for place on the ballot: Monday, August 17, 2026&nbsp;at 5&nbsp;p.m.</li>
	<li>Early voting begins: October 19, 2026</li>
	<li>Last day of early voting: October&nbsp;30, 2026</li>
	<li>Election Date: November 3, 2026</li>
	<li>Notice of Drawing for Place on Ballot:&nbsp;TBD</li>
</ul>

<h3>Application Process</h3>

<ul>
	<li>The candidate filing period to file an application for a place on the ballot is Saturday, July 18, 2026. However, since Wylie ISD offices are not open on this date, the first day the district can receive candidate applications is Monday, July 20, 2026. The last day to file is Monday, August 17, 2026, at 5 p.m.
	<ul>
		<li>Office Hours:<br />
		June 1&nbsp;- July 31, 2026: Monday through Thursday, 7:30 a.m. &ndash; 5 p.m., closed on Fridays.<br />
		Beginning August 3, 2026: Monday through Thursday, 8 a.m. &ndash; 4:30 p.m. or Friday, 8&nbsp;a.m. &ndash; 4 p.m.</li>
	</ul>
	</li>
	<li>All applications filed are public records and open to inspection upon request.</li>
	<li>There is no fee to file a candidate application.</li>
	<li>Completed forms may be returned to the Educational Service Center at 951 S. Ballard Ave., Wylie, TX 75098 or faxed to 972.941.6005, attention Krystal Smith.</li>
</ul>

<p>Wylie ISD warmly welcomes candidates. The Superintendent&rsquo;s Office and the Communications and Community Relations Departments are here to help. To maintain a fair process for all, please know that it is the duty of the candidate to become familiar with the applicable laws regarding campaigns for office. The duty of Wylie ISD is limited to accepting and filing reports and noting the date received thereon. Wylie ISD should not be expected to advise or comment upon the timeliness or sufficiency of reports filed.</p>

<p>For answers to your questions on financial reports, you can contact the Texas Ethics Commission at 800.325.8506. You can find information regarding elections on <a href="http://www.sos.state.tx.us" target="_blank" title="Visit the secretary of state's website for election information. Opens in a new window.">the Secretary of State&rsquo;s website</a>. Information regarding ethics can be found on <a href="http://www.ethics.state.tx.us" target="_blank" title="Visit the Texas ethics commission's website for information on election ethics. Opens in a new window.">the Texas Ethics Commission&rsquo;s website</a>. You can find other helpful information on <a href="http://www.tasb.org" target="_blank" title="Visit the T A S B website for additional election information. Opens in a new window.">the Texas Association of School Boards website</a>,&nbsp;under the board service tab.</p>

<h3>Eligibility/Qualifications</h3>

<p><a aria-label="Policy BBA (LEGAL) - Opens a new window" class="button-2" href="https://pol.tasb.org/Policy/Download/316?filename=BBA(LEGAL).html&amp;title=BOARD%20MEMBERS&amp;subtitle=ELIGIBILITY/QUALIFICATIONS" rel="noopener" target="_blank" title="Link to Wylie ISD eligibility qualifications on TASB website. Opens in a new window.">Policy BBA (LEGAL)</a></p>

<h3>Candidate Resources</h3>

<p><a class="button-1" data-file-name="WylieISD2026FilingPacket.pdf" data-resource-uuid="d5debfcd-a411-49a3-bd8c-2b497b2ed771" href="/fs/resource-manager/view/d5debfcd-a411-49a3-bd8c-2b497b2ed771" target="_blank" title="Candidate Filing Packet in PDF format. Opens in a new window.">Candidate Filing Packet</a></p>

<p><a data-file-name="ApplicationforPlaceonBallot.pdf" data-resource-uuid="773d7462-7499-40af-959d-c86fd5182973" href="/fs/resource-manager/view/773d7462-7499-40af-959d-c86fd5182973" target="_blank"><span class="button-3">application for place on ballot&nbsp;</span></a></p>

<p><a data-file-name="FirstStepsforCandidatesRunningforSchoolBoardTrustee.pdf" data-resource-uuid="e4132d23-0717-4a24-b2b1-74ae1a56e33d" href="/fs/resource-manager/view/e4132d23-0717-4a24-b2b1-74ae1a56e33d" target="_blank"><span class="button-4">First steps to running for school board</span></a></p>

<p><a data-file-name="RequestforConfidentiality.pdf" data-resource-uuid="f601c318-cf5e-48a9-ac2b-8ab65c88ecb4" href="/fs/resource-manager/view/f601c318-cf5e-48a9-ac2b-8ab65c88ecb4" target="_blank"><span class="button-2">request for confidentiality</span></a></p>

<h3>Contact</h3>

<p>Krystal Smith<br />
Assistant to the Superintendent/Board<br />
Wylie ISD<br />
972.429.3005<br />
Fax: 972.941.6005<br />
krystal.smith@wylieisd.net</p>

<div id="candidates">&nbsp;</div>


	</div>


	</section>
	
	<section class="fsElement fsContent" id="fsEl_57948" data-use-new="true" >

				<header>
				<h2 class="fsElementTitle" id="fsElementTitle_57948">2026 Placement on Ballot</h2>
	</header>
	<div class="fsElementContent" >
			<div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 20px; justify-content: center;">
<div style=" width: 100%; max-width: 250px; padding: 15px; border: solid 1px #747679; border-radius: 10px; text-align: center;">
<h3>Place 1</h3>

<p>Stacie Smith</p>
</div>

<div style=" width: 100%; max-width: 250px; padding: 15px; border: solid 1px #747679; border-radius: 10px; text-align: center;">
<h3>Place 2</h3>

<p>Bonnie Tinsley<br />
Brett Fagan<br />
Brandon Thomas<br />
Sam Satterwhite<br />
Scott Johnson</p>
</div>

