	<section class="fsElement fsEmbed" id="fsEl_58155" data-use-new="true" >

				<header>
				<h2 class="fsElementTitle" id="fsElementTitle_58155">Wylie ISD Council of PTAs School Board Candidate Forum</h2>
			<div class="fsElementHeaderContent">
				<p>The Wylie ISD Council of PTAs held a School Board Candidate Forum on Oct. 8, 2026. WRSE invited all five candidates for Wylie ISD Board of Trustees Place 2 to participate; all five candidates attended.</p>

<p>Wylie ISD live streamed and recorded the forum to make it available for public viewing. The video is the full, unedited recording of the forum (lower thirds were added during the live stream).</p>

<p>The candidate forum was organized and hosted by the Council of&nbsp;PTAs. Wylie ISD did not organize or sponsor the forum and does not endorse, support, or oppose any candidate for public office. The district&rsquo;s role was limited to recording and making the unedited forum available for informational purposes.</p>

			</div>
	</header>
	<div class="fsElementContent" >
		    <div class="videoWrapper">
  <iframe allow="autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture" frameborder="0" height="270" sandbox="allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-presentation" scrolling="no" src="https://live.myvrspot.com/iframe?v=YWFhYThiZjZlNzkwYzhkZDY4OWY3MTk1MGZlNjQ0YWM&amp;share=1" width="480"></iframe>
</div>

	</div>


	</section>
	
	<section class="fsElement fsContent" id="fsEl_57972" data-use-new="true" >

				<header>
				<h2 class="fsElementTitle" id="fsElementTitle_57972">Wylie Retired School Employees School Board Candidate Forum</h2>
	</header>
	<div class="fsElementContent" >
			<p>The Wylie Retired School Employees (WRSE) held a School Board Candidate Forum during its Sept. 9, 2026, meeting. WRSE invited all five candidates for Wylie ISD Board of Trustees Place 2 to participate; four candidates attended.</p>

<p>Wylie ISD recorded the forum to make it available for public viewing. The video is the full, unedited recording of the forum.</p>

<p>The candidate forum was organized and hosted by WRSE. Wylie ISD did not organize or sponsor the forum and does not endorse, support, or oppose any candidate for public office. The district&rsquo;s role was limited to recording and making the unedited forum available for informational purposes.</p>

<div class="videoWrapper"><iframe allow="autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture" frameborder="0" height="270" sandbox="allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-presentation" scrolling="no" src="https://live.myvideospot.com/iframe?v=NTAxMTg0NmRkNGJhZjAxNWJmMjU1MTQ2OTc1Y2MyYzk&amp;share=1" width="480"></iframe></div>


	</div>


	</section>
	



